Portions of the Backup app reimplement concepts from Seedvault, the encrypted
backup application for Android:

    https://github.com/seedvault-app/seedvault

Seedvault's application code is distributed under the Apache License 2.0. The
ported concepts here are the recovery-code scheme (a BIP-0039 12-word mnemonic
deriving a 512-bit seed via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512), the segmented AES-256-GCM
on-disk backup format, and the overall app-data backup transport design. This
is an independent Kotlin reimplementation, not a copy of Seedvault's source, but
attribution is retained per the established convention in this repository (see
networklocation/src/main/rust/LICENSE-GrapheneOS).

The BIP-0039 English wordlist bundled at
backup/src/main/resources/bip39-english.txt is the canonical list from the
Bitcoin BIPs repository (public domain / BSD-2-Clause):

    https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039/english.txt

